// Shared type-checker config for BOTH basedpyright (the CLI gate, see
// README.md) and plain Pyright, which is what most editors run as their
// language server.
//
// It can't live in pyproject.toml: basedpyright refuses a file containing both
// [tool.pyright] and [tool.basedpyright] ("pick one"), so a plain-Pyright
// editor would get no `extraPaths` and report a spurious
// `reportMissingImports` on every first-party import. This file is read by
// both tools and takes precedence over pyproject.toml.
//
// `typeCheckingMode: "recommended"` is basedpyright-only; plain Pyright notes
// that it doesn't recognise the value and falls back to its own default.
//
// `ignore` covers Django's generated migrations: `makemigrations` writes
// `settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL` (typed `Any`, since django-stubs resolves custom
// settings through `LazySettings.__getattr__`), so every regeneration would
// otherwise reintroduce `reportAny` warnings that can't be fixed in-file.
{
  "typeCheckingMode": "recommended",
  "ignore": ["src/backend/**/migrations/"],
  "venvPath": ".",
  "venv": ".venv",
  "extraPaths": ["src/backend"]
}
